            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.248,
            0.69,
            0.849,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The values of volume are obtained in units of mL, which can be written in the equivalent unit cm"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3",
              "styles": [
                "superscript"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " for solids."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.252,
            0.748,
            0.884,
            0.807
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "We have already learnt to measure the mass and volume of liquids and solids of different types. These quantities can be used to calculate the density of the object or the substance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.809,
            0.576,
            0.83
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us calculate the density"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.832,
            0.788,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Density can be calculated using the following formula:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "equation",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.338,
            0.858,
            0.765,
            0.898
          ],
          "image_path": "images/page_12_equation_17.jpg",
          "content": "\\mathrm{Density} = \\frac{\\mathrm{Mass}}{\\mathrm{Volum}} = \\frac{16.400\\ \\mathrm{g}}{5\\ \\mathrm{cm}^3} = 3.28\\ \\mathrm{g/cm}^3"
        },
